<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19609" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">glaebālis</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">glēb-</span></b> ), e, adj.
		glaeba. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>relating to clods</i>
			(post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agger,</span>”
				<i>consisting of clods</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 23, 5, 15</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			law Lat. (acc. to glaeba, II. A.), <i>of</i> or <i>relating to lands</i>: collatio, <i>a
				tax paid from</i>
			
			<i>lands</i>, <i>land-tax</i>, Cod. Th.
			6, 2, 3; 4, 8, 11 et saep.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
